1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,123
GameStudio's kits make game-ready props:

2
00:00:06,210 --> 00:00:09,559
rocks, crates, barrels, trees, fences and more.

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,469
They're not in Blender's Add menu:

4
00:00:11,469 --> 00:00:13,542
you ask for them in Claude Code.

5
00:00:13,744 --> 00:00:14,220
Here:

6
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:17,768
a crate, a barrel, a mossy rock and a pine tree.

7
00:00:18,333 --> 00:00:19,471
Claude checks the kits and

8
00:00:19,471 --> 00:00:21,207
builds all four in your level.

9
00:00:21,352 --> 00:00:24,388
Each one is a finished model, standing on the lawn.

10
00:00:24,967 --> 00:00:26,732
To change one, select it first.

11
00:00:26,732 --> 00:00:27,957
Click the rock.

12
00:00:28,533 --> 00:00:30,223
Then say what to change.

13
00:00:30,263 --> 00:00:31,929
Claude sees what you selected.

14
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:34,542
Make this rock bigger, with a different shape.

15
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:36,911
It rebuilds the rock from its kit

16
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:39,065
with a new size and a new seed.

17
00:00:39,210 --> 00:00:40,696
The seed picks the shape,

18
00:00:40,696 --> 00:00:43,756
and the same seed always gives the same rock.

19
00:00:44,333 --> 00:00:45,883
Next, click the barrel.

20
00:00:46,833 --> 00:00:47,954
Now a colour.

21
00:00:47,994 --> 00:00:50,188
The kits share one material palette:

22
00:00:50,188 --> 00:00:52,568
stone, woods, metals, brick and more.

23
00:00:52,568 --> 00:00:54,560
Paint this barrel brick red.

24
00:00:55,133 --> 00:00:56,143
Claude gives the barrel's

25
00:00:56,143 --> 00:00:57,914
wood the palette's brick red.

26
00:00:57,954 --> 00:01:00,538
The iron hoops and the lid stay as they were.

27
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:03,579
In the Properties, open the Material tab.

28
00:01:03,666 --> 00:01:04,636
There it is:

29
00:01:04,722 --> 00:01:07,875
G S Brick, the palette's shared brick material.

30
00:01:07,961 --> 00:01:09,169
Change it here, and every

31
00:01:09,169 --> 00:01:11,102
prop that uses it follows.

32
00:01:11,667 --> 00:01:13,130
Claude places props, too.

33
00:01:13,130 --> 00:01:13,513
Say:

34
00:01:13,513 --> 00:01:15,307
now put it on top of the crate.

35
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:18,356
It moves the barrel over the crate

36
00:01:18,356 --> 00:01:20,434
and snaps it onto the first surface below,

37
00:01:20,434 --> 00:01:22,507
so nothing floats or sinks.

38
00:01:22,593 --> 00:01:25,781
The same snap sets props on hills and slopes.

39
00:01:26,333 --> 00:01:29,549
For a last look, turn on Game in the 3D View's header,

40
00:01:29,549 --> 00:01:32,109
to see the props the way the game draws them.

41
00:01:32,667 --> 00:01:33,352
That's it:

42
00:01:33,352 --> 00:01:35,964
ask for props from the kits, change their size,

43
00:01:35,964 --> 00:01:37,724
seed or colour, and place them.

44
00:01:37,996 --> 00:01:40,626
Every change Claude makes can be undone.
